cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "Code for: Error law and tolerance limits of the Kirchhoff approximation on two-scale dielectric surfaces, with boundary-variation corrections"
abstract: >-
  Python code and cached data behind the figure, the tables and the numbers of the paper, and the validation scripts. The paper gives the
  error law of the Kirchhoff approximation (KA, an expansion in the curvature of the surface) against its validity parameter C and the
  slope of the roughness, and the limits of C for a tolerated error, for one-dimensional lossless dielectric surfaces made of a smooth
  periodic profile carrying a small-scale roughness (TE and TM), against an independent C-method reference with energy conservation as a
  check. A boundary-variation series (the method of variation of boundaries, an expansion in the height, taken about the periodic
  surface, with the Kirchhoff amplitudes or the exact solution of the smooth profile as zeroth order) is used to measure how far the
  small scale can be added to the smooth-profile solution.
